# peartree-genotype2 config for GRCh38 colony BAMs WITH the reference-bias profile: the base config
# plus the per-locus het likelihood at a grid of reference-bias values b (pl_het_b400 .. pl_het_b1000
# columns). Calls in the per-colony files are unchanged (ref_bias stays 1); the joint step's
# `--ref-bias auto` estimates b from germline-het loci (global, per locus kind, per colony) and
# plugs it into each colony's het likelihood. See rust/peartree-genotype2/README.md "Reference bias".
include = config.genotype2.grch38
# The grid's ends CLAMP the joint estimate (joint.rs cell_b / interp_profile): PD51635 measured
# b = 1.248 (ALT over-captured) and got no correction at all with a grid ending at 1.0, hence
# 1.1 / 1.25 / 1.5. Nothing here is assembly-specific (GRCh37 runs use this file too).
ref_bias_grid = 0.4,0.5,0.6,0.7,0.8,0.9,1.0,1.1,1.25,1.5
# a FIXED correction of the per-colony calls themselves (b, or per kind) would be e.g.
#   ref_bias = 0.9
#   ref_bias_kind = L1_MED_DELETION:0.6
